IMPORT prelude

-- Newfoundland and Labrador Income and Employment Support Act (SNL2002 cI-0.1) and Income and Employment Support
-- Regulations (NLR 144/04), Part I -- income support for a household in the province: who can get it (Act ss 13, 15,
-- regs ss 4, 9), the liquid-asset limits (reg s 26), the income that counts and its exemptions (regs ss 8, 11, 12), the
-- monthly amounts (regs ss 13, 16, 18, 19(1)), and what the person must report (Act s 17(5), reg s 7(1)). The time
-- limits (reg s 5(2), Act ss 41(3), 43(2)) are in nl-ies-deadlines.l4.
--
-- SEAT: the applicant or recipient of income support. "Can I get income support? How much a month at most? What must
-- I report, and by when must I answer, ask for a review or appeal?" Officers, the minister and the appeal board appear
-- only as what they may do to the person or must give them.
--
-- Edition: the House of Assembly consolidations retrieved 2026-10-24: the Act as amended to 2019 cS-29.02 s27 (sections
-- 2, 13 to 17, 41 and 43 deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SNL2002-cI-0.1-selected.txt) and the Regulations as
-- amended to 106/25 (Part I and s 45 at ../../registers/source-bundle/NLR-144-04-part-i.txt).
--
-- The amounts in regs ss 13, 16 and 19 are "up to" amounts: an officer grants income support "according to the Act,
-- these regulations, and any policies, procedures and service standards established by the minister" (reg s 6(3)(a)).
-- The encoding computes the most the regulations allow; what is granted may be less.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: employment support (Part II of the Regulations); special needs (regs ss 21 to 24), the start-up
-- allowance (s 17), funeral costs (s 27), emergencies (s 28), hospital and shelter amounts (s 19(2) to (4)), the
-- other s 19(1) and (5) amounts that are set by an officer or the minister; overpayments and recovery (Act Part III);
-- the lump-sum rules (reg s 10); the under-21 rules (reg s 18(2) to (4)); emergency eligibility (Act s 16).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income and Employment Support -- income support for a household`

§§ `Small arithmetic`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`zero or more` x MEANS IF x GREATER THAN 0 THEN x ELSE 0

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

§§ `Act s 15 and reg s 4 -- living in the province`

-- Act s 15(1): "An applicant and a recipient shall live in the province to be eligible"; (2): "live in the province"
-- means physically present, but a person may be temporarily absent for a prescribed purpose. Reg s 4(2): a recipient
-- may be absent "(a) for a period of up to 60 days for a purpose approved by an officer; or (b) for a period of more
-- than 60 days if the absence is due to medical reasons and is approved by an officer". The approval is the officer's;
-- it is asked as a fact ("if an officer has approved ...").
GIVEN `physically present in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days absent` IS A NUMBER
      `an officer approved the purpose of the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the absence is for medical reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lives in the province` IF
        `physically present in the province`
    OR  (    `an officer approved the purpose of the absence`
         AND (   `days absent` AT MOST 60
              OR `the absence is for medical reasons`))

§§ `Act s 13 and reg s 9 -- the conditions of eligibility`

-- Act s 13(1): "as a condition of eligibility for income support, a person shall pursue all other financial resources
-- available to him or her or his or her spouse or cohabiting partner" (not including support under s 38 of the Family
-- Law Act, s 13(2)). Reg s 9(5): "where an applicant is applying for income support due to job action at the
-- workplace, the applicant shall not be eligible".
GIVEN `lives in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has pursued all other financial resources` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applying because of job action at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the conditions of eligibility` IF
        `lives in the province`
    AND `has pursued all other financial resources`
    AND (NOT `applying because of job action at the workplace`)

§§ `Reg s 26 -- liquid assets`

-- Reg s 26(1): income support may be granted where liquid assets "do not exceed ... (a) for one person, $6,000; and
-- (b) for 2 or more people, combined liquid assets of $11,000". The "people" are read as the persons the application is
-- for: the applicant, a spouse or cohabiting partner (Act s 2(d)) and dependants (NOTES.md finding 3).
-- s 26(3), (4): RRSPs "with a cumulative value of $20,000 or less are exempt"; above that, "the value ... in excess of
-- $20,000 shall, where the Registered Retirement Savings Plans may be liquefied, be considered a liquid asset".
-- s 8(b): liquid assets are cash and readily marketable securities, not counting RESPs, a support trust, prepaid
-- funeral funds, exempt income and a severance package during its covering period; those are left out of the input.
GIVEN `people in the application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the liquid asset limit` MEANS IF `people in the application` AT MOST 1 THEN 6000 ELSE 11000

GIVEN `liquid assets other than RRSPs` IS A NUMBER
      `value of RRSPs` IS A NUMBER
      `the RRSPs can be cashed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the liquid assets counted` MEANS
    `liquid assets other than RRSPs`
    PLUS (IF `the RRSPs can be cashed` THEN `zero or more` (`value of RRSPs` MINUS 20000) ELSE 0)

GIVEN `people in the application` IS A NUMBER
      `liquid assets counted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `liquid assets are within the limit` IF
    `liquid assets counted` AT MOST (`the liquid asset limit` `people in the application`)

§§ `Regs ss 8, 11, 12 -- the income that counts`

-- s 12(a): exemptions from earnings (salary, wages, self-employment) and winnings, "in the month it is received":
-- (i) single adult: 100% up to $75 plus 20% above; (ii) 2 or more persons: $150; (iii) a person requiring supportive
-- services: $150; (iv) 2 or more persons where at least one requires supportive services: $250.
DECLARE `Exemption class` IS ONE OF
    `a single adult`
    `two or more persons`
    `a person requiring supportive services`
    `two or more persons, one requiring supportive services`

GIVEN `people in the application` IS A NUMBER
      `someone requires supportive services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Exemption class`
`the exemption class` MEANS
    IF `people in the application` AT MOST 1
    THEN IF `someone requires supportive services` THEN `a person requiring supportive services` ELSE `a single adult`
    ELSE IF `someone requires supportive services` THEN `two or more persons, one requiring supportive services` ELSE `two or more persons`

GIVEN `class` IS AN `Exemption class`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fully exempt part` `class` MEANS
    CONSIDER `class`
    WHEN `a single adult` THEN 75
    WHEN `two or more persons` THEN 150
    WHEN `a person requiring supportive services` THEN 150
    WHEN `two or more persons, one requiring supportive services` THEN 250

GIVEN `class` IS AN `Exemption class`, `earnings in the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 12(a) exemption` MEANS
    LET base MEANS `the fully exempt part` `class`
    IN  (`the lesser of` `earnings in the month` base) PLUS (20% TIMES (`zero or more` (`earnings in the month` MINUS base)))

-- s 18(1): the officer "shall deduct from the total income support to which the applicant or recipient is entitled
-- under section 13 and section 16 ... (a) all non-exempt income; and (b) all partially exempt income minus (i) the
-- deduction described in section 11, and (ii) the exemptions described in section 12". The s 11 deduction (expenses of
-- earning the income) is one an officer "may authorize"; it is asked as the amount authorized.
GIVEN `class` IS AN `Exemption class`
      `earnings in the month` IS A NUMBER
      `authorized expenses of earning` IS A NUMBER
      `non-exempt income in the month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income deducted` MEANS
        `non-exempt income in the month`
    PLUS `zero or more` ((`earnings in the month` MINUS `authorized expenses of earning`) MINUS (`the s 12(a) exemption` `class` `earnings in the month`))

§§ `Regs ss 13 and 16 -- the monthly amounts for living costs and shelter`

-- s 13(1): "The monthly amount of income support for each adult who is boarding, renting or owns a residence is an
-- amount up to $561." s 13(2): reduced where heat or electricity is included: in an apartment or house by $76 (both),
-- $49 (heat only) or $27 (electricity only); in a bed sitting room by $61, $49 or $12.
DECLARE `Dwelling` IS ONE OF
    `an apartment or a house`
    `a bed sitting room`

DECLARE `Utilities included` IS ONE OF
    `heat and electricity`
    `heat only`
    `electricity only`
    `neither`

GIVEN `dwelling` IS A `Dwelling`, `included` IS A `Utilities included`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 13(2) reduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `included`
    WHEN `heat and electricity` THEN IF `in a bed sitting room` THEN 61 ELSE 76
    WHEN `heat only` THEN 49
    WHEN `electricity only` THEN IF `in a bed sitting room` THEN 12 ELSE 27
    WHEN `neither` THEN 0
    WHERE
        `in a bed sitting room` MEANS `dwelling` EQUALS `a bed sitting room`

GIVEN `adults` IS A NUMBER, `dwelling` IS A `Dwelling`, `included` IS A `Utilities included`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 13 amount` MEANS `zero or more` ((561 TIMES `adults`) MINUS (`the s 13(2) reduction` `dwelling` `included`))

-- s 16(1): the maximum for rent, or for principal and interest on a mortgage on the principal residence, is "(i) for an
-- adult living alone or with a dependent ... up to $522, or (ii) for 2 or more adults ... up to $299 for each adult".
-- s 16(2): where s 13(2) reduced the support, these maximums "are increased by the amount of the deductions ... but in
-- no case shall the total amount exceed the actual amount required by the applicant or recipient for shelter".
DECLARE `Shelter` IS ONE OF
    `renting`
    `paying a mortgage`
    `boarding`
    `no shelter cost`

GIVEN `adults` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 16(1) maximum` `adults` MEANS IF `adults` AT MOST 1 THEN 522 ELSE 299 TIMES `adults`

GIVEN `shelter` IS A `Shelter`
      `adults` IS A NUMBER
      `monthly rent or mortgage payment` IS A NUMBER
      `dwelling` IS A `Dwelling`
      `included` IS A `Utilities included`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 16 amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `shelter`
    WHEN `renting` THEN `capped`
    WHEN `paying a mortgage` THEN `capped`
    OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        `capped` MEANS `the lesser of` (`zero or more` `monthly rent or mortgage payment`) ((`the s 16(1) maximum` `adults`) PLUS (`the s 13(2) reduction` `dwelling` `included`))

§§ `Reg s 19(1) -- other monthly amounts`

-- s 19(1) "Other monthly income support for which an applicant or recipient may be eligible is": (a) a fuel supplement
-- "up to a maximum of $132" in Labrador, (b) "up to a maximum of $71" on the island, "where the cost of heat is not
-- included in the amount of rent"; (f) "$105 for each applicant or recipient who is 65 years of age or older" (unless
-- they will stop being eligible within 2 months); (h) "for a recipient maintaining a residence in a coastal Labrador
-- community, an amount of $150"; (i) "$89 for each recipient or dependent ... who is legally blind"; (j) "$60 for each
-- recipient or dependent with diabetes" (each certified); (p) "for an applicant or recipient who has a dependent but
-- does not have a spouse or cohabiting partner, an amount of $168". Only these fixed amounts are encoded; (c) to (e),
-- (g), (k), (l), (n), (o) depend on an officer's or the minister's determination or a one-off event.
DECLARE `Region` IS ONE OF
    `the island portion of the province`
    `Labrador, outside the coastal communities`
    `a coastal Labrador community`

GIVEN `region` IS A `Region`
      `maintains a residence where heat is not included in the rent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adults 65 or older who will stay eligible` IS A NUMBER
      `persons certified legally blind` IS A NUMBER
      `persons certified with diabetes` IS A NUMBER
      `has a dependent and no spouse or cohabiting partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 19(1) amounts` MEANS
        `fuel`
    PLUS (105 TIMES `adults 65 or older who will stay eligible`)
    PLUS `coastal`
    PLUS (89 TIMES `persons certified legally blind`)
    PLUS (60 TIMES `persons certified with diabetes`)
    PLUS (IF `has a dependent and no spouse or cohabiting partner` THEN 168 ELSE 0)
    WHERE
        `fuel` MEANS
            IF `maintains a residence where heat is not included in the rent`
            THEN IF `region` EQUALS `the island portion of the province` THEN 71 ELSE 132
            ELSE 0
        `coastal` MEANS
            IF `region` EQUALS `a coastal Labrador community` THEN 150 ELSE 0

§§ `Reg s 18(1) -- the monthly income support`

-- The most a month: the ss 13 and 16 amounts less the income deducted under s 18(1), never below nil, plus the
-- s 19(1) amounts. Section 18(1) deducts income only from the "income support to which the applicant or recipient is
-- entitled under section 13 and section 16"; it does not reach s 19 (NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `s 13 and s 16 amounts` IS A NUMBER, `income deducted` IS A NUMBER, `s 19(1) amounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most monthly income support` MEANS
    (`zero or more` (`s 13 and s 16 amounts` MINUS `income deducted`)) PLUS `s 19(1) amounts`

§§ `Reg s 9(3) -- the applicant's income test`

-- s 9(3): eligibility is determined "by evaluating the applicant's financial situation for the 30 days preceding the
-- date of application according to the following formula: BR + (.40 x BR) + CBA is >= I - D", where BR is the s 13(1)
-- amount plus the s 16(1)(a) or (b) amount if applicable, CBA the child benefit adjustment (an amount the minister
-- approves: s 19(1)(g)), I "the applicant's total net income calculated according to paragraphs 8(c) and 8(d) minus the
-- deduction for expenses incurred in earning that income referred to in section 11" and D "the deduction referred to in
-- section 11". Read as written, the s 11 deduction is subtracted twice (NOTES.md finding 5).
GIVEN `BR` IS A NUMBER, `CBA` IS A NUMBER, `net income in the 30 days` IS A NUMBER, `s 11 deduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `passes the s 9(3) income test` IF
    (`BR` PLUS (40% TIMES `BR`) PLUS `CBA`) AT LEAST ((`net income in the 30 days` MINUS `s 11 deduction`) MINUS `s 11 deduction`)

GIVEN `adults` IS A NUMBER
      `shelter` IS A `Shelter`
      `monthly rent or mortgage payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`BR for the s 9(3) test` MEANS
        (561 TIMES `adults`)
    PLUS `the shelter part`
    WHERE
        `the shelter part` MEANS
            IF `shelter` EQUALS `renting` OR `shelter` EQUALS `paying a mortgage`
            THEN `the lesser of` (`zero or more` `monthly rent or mortgage payment`) (`the s 16(1) maximum` `adults`)
            ELSE 0

§§ `Act s 17(5) and reg s 7(1) -- what must be reported`

-- Act s 17(5): "A recipient shall notify the officer immediately of any changes that may affect that recipient's
-- eligibility". Reg s 7(1) lists them: (a) address; (b) living arrangements; (c) marital or cohabitation status; (d)
-- the circumstances of any dependents; (e) income, liquid assets, real property or assets; (f) absence from the
-- province; (g) the reason for the application; (h) receipt of a liquid asset; (i) sale or transfer of assets; (j)
-- expenses of earning income; (k) any other circumstance the minister determines. Under reg s 7(2) an officer "may
-- deny, vary, suspend or cancel income support where a circumstance ... has been confirmed".
DECLARE `Change` IS ONE OF
    `my address`
    `my living arrangements`
    `my marital or cohabitation status`
    `the circumstances of a dependent`
    `my income, liquid assets, real property or assets`
    `an absence from the province`
    `the reason I applied`
    `I received a liquid asset`
    `I sold or transferred an asset or real property`
    `my expenses of earning income`
    `something the minister has said must be reported`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `change` IS A `Change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change must be reported immediately` IF
    CONSIDER `change`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
